            <ArticleTitle>Unstable anginal syndrome and pulmonary oedema due to thyrotoxicosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a 40 year old woman who presented with typical unstable angina pectoris associated with pulmonary oedema, due to poorly controlled hyperthyroidism. No cardiac abnormality was detected by echo-Doppler and nuclear ventriculography. Coronary angiography demonstrated normal coronary arteries. This case represents a new manifestation of the known association of cardiac ischaemia with hyperthyroidism in the presence of normal coronary arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
